  "body": "## What is wrong\n\nIn `assets/posts/tormach.cps` on main (after PR #2386), a rapid or linear record that has no A angle gets `a = 0`.\nIf the indexed operation has an A angle that is not 0, the post writes a `G0` or `G1` block with an `A0` word.\nBefore PR #2386, the post refused this record.\nA turn to A0 in the middle of an indexed operation moves the work under the tool. That can be a collision or a cut in the wrong place.\n\n## Reading (source only, not built, not run)\n\n1. A record with no A gets `a = 0`: `tormach.cps:691-698`. With a section angle that is not 0, the difference is `-aSection`: `tormach.cps:709-713`.\n2. `onRapid` (`:1039`) and `onLinear` (`:1046`) call `motionFor(properties, \"\")`. The empty name skips the refusal at `:715-716`. The move becomes `aNext = {a: 0}` (`:725`).\n3. `turnMove` (`:862-910`) writes the block with the `A0` word (`:888`, `:892`, `:895`, `:907-909`).\n4. Arcs, probe moves and canned cycles pass a name, and the post refuses them at `:716`.\n5. The engine adds A only when the CL record has an A word: `crates/post/src/post/cnc.rs:194-198`. It does not fill A from the section.\n\n## Not confirmed\n\n- It is not confirmed that the toolpath stream can emit a record without an A angle inside an indexed operation whose angle is not 0. If it cannot, the defect cannot occur today, but no test or refusal guards it.\n- It is not confirmed that a turn to A0 is the intended reading of such a record.\n\n## Tests\n\nNo test was found for a record without A in an indexed section. Checked by name: `tormach_wrapped_a.rs`, `tormach_fourth_axis.rs`, `fourth_axis_pose.rs`.\n\n## Source\n\nThe read-only Opus review of the merged PR #2386, and a source reading after it:\nhttps://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2386#issuecomment-6972209368\n\n## Done when\n\n- The first step confirms if the stream can emit such a record, with a recorded `.cl` file.\n- A record without an A angle in an indexed operation keeps the section angle, or the post refuses it with a diagnostic. It does not turn A silently.\n- A test pins the result for a rapid record and for a linear record.\n",
